      "problem": "What is $\\frac{10g+30}{8g+24}$ reduced to its lowest terms?",
      "worked_solution": "We factor the numerator and denominator and cancel any factors that they have in common.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{10g+30}{8g+24} & =\\frac{5(2g+6)}{4(2g+6)} \\\\  & =\\frac{5\\cancel{(2g+6)}}{4\\cancel{(2g+6)}} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
